.TH TAG 1
.SH NAME
tag, tags, untag \- a file's attributes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tag
.I file key\fB=\fPvalue
.br
.B tags
.I file
.br
.B untag
.I file key
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
Any object on SieFS can carry attributes, for example
.BR "project = SIEOS" .
.B tag
sets the attribute
.I key
of
.I file
to
.IR value ;
.B tags
lists all of them as
.IB key = value
lines;
.B untag
removes one.
.PP
An attribute whose value is at most 255 bytes is also indexed, so
.BR find (1)
finds every file with it without reading the others. The desktop's
projects are built on them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure ("no such attribute" for an unknown key).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tag notes.txt project=SIEOS
tags notes.txt
find project=SIEOS
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR siefs (5)
.SH BUGS
Values up to 1024 bytes;
.B tags
shows at most 4096 bytes of names.
